// Parameter table: Panasonic AW-UE160 (HTTP CGI integrated-camera protocol).
//
// One entry per row of the spec notes' parameter table (section 10a: the
// camera's own menu/command table, IF = "HD/4K Integrated Camera Interface
// Specifications — AW-UE160", Mar. 1 2025; section 10b: the web CGIs, WEB =
// "Supplement for Web Control" Ver. 1.09). `wire.src` on every entry cites the
// page; CPZ = the Bitfocus companion-module-panasonic-ptz, which only covers the
// sibling AW-UE150 (its camdata dump is from a UE150).
//
// Generated once from the notes' table and then checked by hand, which is why
// it is one entry per line. A few rows became several entries because one
// command addresses several things by index (audio inputs/outputs, the four
// pan/tilt limits, scene/user file names, preset speed in its two units).
//
// `wire` (private to the driver):
//   path   'cam' → /cgi-bin/aw_cam?cmd=…&res=1, 'ptz' → /cgi-bin/aw_ptz?cmd=%23…&res=1,
//          'cgi' → a web CGI (`get` / `set` URL, `key` in its key=value reply,
//          `summary` = show every key (or those matching the regex) read-only)
//   q      query command;  r  reply prefix (data follows);  alt  other prefixes
//          the same value arrives under in /live/camdata.html or a push
//   s      set prefix (data follows);  echo  what a write-only command answers
//   push   the spec's "Update notification" column says the camera pushes it
//   codec  how data ↔ value: bool (f/t codes), enum (option value = wire code,
//          compared numerically in `base`), map (separate write/read codes),
//          lin (value = a·n + b, n in `base`, `w` digits; `special` codes are
//          words such as "AGC ON"), band (#UPVS speed bands), ascii (hex pairs,
//          fixed length), raw (as sent), bits (error bit masks)
//   param  an action's numeric payload (`off` added before encoding: presets are
//          sent as number − 1);  textParam  an action's text payload pattern;
//          data  an action's fixed data
//   via    the row is reached some other way and not offered as a setting:
//          'motion' (joystick with deadman, Home), 'presets', 'push', or 'none'
//          (with the reason in `help`)
//
// Option values are the camera's own codes ("0", "1", "0A"): they mean nothing
// to a person, and the labels — the camera menu's words — carry the meaning.
// Labels are the menu's own capitals, as the camera's menu and web page show them.

